  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.0 has breaking changes. A crashed transaction no longer blocks the whole work folder, and the names of staging entries are reserved.\n\n- The static entry class Txfio is now TxFileIO (TxFileIO.BeginAsync, TxFileIO.RecoverAsync), so the calls compile after `using Txfio;`.\n- Do not share a work folder between 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 clients.\n- RecoveryRequiredException comes from staging and CommitAsync for overlapping paths only, not from BeginAsync. RecoverAsync runs while other transactions are alive and reports RecoverResult.Contended.\n- CreateDirectoryAsync reserves its directory until the transaction ends.\n- Paths with a staging name ({name}.{txid}.txnew, .txnew.prev, .txold) throw InvalidOperationException. Listings and copies skip every transaction's staging entries. New: TxFileIO.IsStagingName.\n- A directory DeleteAsync conflict names the blocking child in ExternalConflictException.Path.\n\nFull notes and how to move: https://github.com/YUKIKEDA/Txfio/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
